WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.082
Use a consistent identity model across local services, cloud accounts, gateways, storage,

00:00:05.082 --> 00:00:05.913
and applications.

00:00:05.913 --> 00:00:10.064
Grant least privilege and require authentication at every exposed endpoint.

00:00:10.064 --> 00:00:11.725
Segment management, model-serving, storage,

00:00:11.725 --> 00:00:16.707
and user traffic so compromise of a front end does not provide

00:00:16.707 --> 00:00:19.614
unrestricted access to private data or infrastructure.

00:00:19.614 --> 00:00:24.596
Store provider keys, model tokens, and service credentials in managed secrets systems.

00:00:24.596 --> 00:00:29.578
Rotate them, restrict their scope, and prevent them from entering prompts, images,

00:00:29.578 --> 00:00:30.824
repositories, or logs.

00:00:30.824 --> 00:00:34.560
Patch local operating systems, GPU drivers, runtimes, gateways, containers,

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:37.051
and cloud components through controlled releases.

00:00:37.051 --> 00:00:42.449
Hybrid systems have a larger dependency surface, so version inventory and rollback matter.

00:00:42.449 --> 00:00:46.186
Audit routing decisions, configuration changes, authentication, administrative actions, costs,

00:00:46.186 --> 00:00:47.846
errors, and security events.

00:00:47.846 --> 00:00:54.074
Minimize sensitive prompt and output content in logs while preserving enough evidence to investigate incidents.

00:00:54.074 --> 00:00:59.056
Correlate local and cloud timestamps and request identifiers so an end-to-end event

00:00:59.056 --> 00:01:03.623
can be reconstructed without copying private data into every monitoring system.

00:01:03.623 --> 00:01:07.775
Prepare incident procedures for data misrouting, exposed credentials, provider outage,

00:01:07.775 --> 00:01:10.266
compromised local nodes, and unexpected spending.

00:01:10.266 --> 00:01:15.249
Define how to disable a route, revoke keys, isolate systems, preserve evidence,

00:01:15.249 --> 00:01:17.740
restore configuration, and communicate degraded capability.

00:01:17.740 --> 00:01:21.476
Back up irreplaceable data and policy, and test rollback.

00:01:21.476 --> 00:01:23.552
Review vendor security, availability, retention,

00:01:23.552 --> 00:01:28.119
and exit options because provider risk is part of the architecture,

00:01:28.119 --> 00:01:29.780
not an external footnote.
